From 370d716175843cc5aabb075a9255c88fdd3b584c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rubens-port <rubens-port@localhost>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:28:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rubens port fixes on top of 80d38270aa

Carried over from the previous snapshot tree so the Ubuntu 26.04 port keeps
working on the newer upstream baseline:

  * mt6895-xiaomi-rubens.dts / -xaga.dts: the port's board adjustments
  * drivers/misc/rubens-bootlog.c: bootlog target lookup that survives
    initmem being freed (upstream added its own fix in 4c23dbfdd2; this is
    the locally verified variant)
  * tools/build-rubens-bootimg*.sh: the LK-safe boot.img packers

Committing them (rather than leaving the tree dirty) also keeps
scripts/setlocalversion from appending '+' to the kernel release, which would
have made uname -r '7.2.0+' and orphaned every module in /lib/modules/7.2.0.
---
